        "title": "Introduction",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Remember that in order to add fractions with different denominators, like <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac 1 4 + \\dfrac 1 8,]</span> we need to put the fractions over a <strong>common denominator</strong>, as follows:</p>",
            "readable_text": "Remember that in order to add fractions with different denominators, like [MATH: \\dfrac 1 4 + \\dfrac 1 8,] we need to put the fractions over a common denominator, as follows:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: (1)/(4) + (1)/(8)|=; (2)/(8) + (1)/(8)|=; (3)/(8)]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: (1)/(4) + (1)/(8)|=; (2)/(8) + (1)/(8)|=; (3)/(8)]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>It works the same in algebra! To add two fractions, we need to put each fraction over a common denominator. Then, we add the numerators.</p>",
            "readable_text": "It works the same in algebra! To add two fractions, we need to put each fraction over a common denominator. Then, we add the numerators.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nRemember that in order to add fractions with different denominators, like [MATH: \\dfrac 1 4 + \\dfrac 1 8,] we need to put the fractions over a common denominator, as follows:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: (1)/(4) + (1)/(8)|=; (2)/(8) + (1)/(8)|=; (3)/(8)]\n\nContent:\nIt works the same in algebra! To add two fractions, we need to put each fraction over a common denominator. Then, we add the numerators."
      },
